X('what-is-a-freight-forwarder',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>Consolidation:</b> combining several small shipments into one container or one airway bill.','<b>Co-loading:</b> a forwarder buying space from another forwarder.','<b>Door to door:</b> the forwarder handles pickup, carriage and delivery.','<b>Cut-off:</b> the last time the cargo or documents are accepted for a sailing or flight.','<b>Consignee and notify party:</b> who receives the cargo and who is told it has arrived.'])])
X('how-to-choose-a-freight-forwarder',[('What good service looks like',['You get a quote the same day, with every charge shown. You get the draft bill of lading before the vessel sails. You are told about a delay before you have to ask. Someone answers the phone when the cargo is held at the port. These are small things, and they separate forwarders more than price does.'])])
X('customs-broker-role-and-licence',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>CHA:</b> customs house agent, the old name for a customs broker.','<b>CBLR:</b> the Customs Brokers Licensing Regulations that govern the licence.','<b>F card and G card:</b> identity cards for authorised persons of the broker, used for different kinds of work at the customs house.','<b>ICEGATE:</b> the customs e-commerce portal where filing and payment are done.'])])
X('bill-of-entry-explained',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>Assessment:</b> working out the duty on the bill, by the system or by an officer.','<b>Self-assessment:</b> the importer works out the duty and the officer verifies it.','<b>Out of charge:</b> the order that clears the goods for release.','<b>Prior filing:</b> filing the bill before the cargo arrives.','<b>Amendment:</b> a change to a bill already filed.'])])
X('how-customs-duty-is-calculated-in-india',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>BCD:</b> basic customs duty, the main duty on the HS code.','<b>SWS:</b> social welfare surcharge, charged on the duty.','<b>IGST:</b> the integrated goods and services tax on imports, which an importer can usually claim as credit.','<b>CIF:</b> cost, insurance and freight, the usual start of the assessable value.','<b>Notification:</b> a government order that changes a rate or grants an exemption.'])])
X('air-freight-chargeable-weight-and-rates',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>Chargeable weight:</b> the greater of actual and volumetric weight.','<b>Minimum charge:</b> the smallest amount the airline accepts for a shipment.','<b>Weight break:</b> the weight at which the rate per kg falls.','<b>Surcharge:</b> fuel, security or other additions to the base rate.','<b>ULD:</b> unit load device, the pallet or container the airline loads.'])])
X('air-freight-booking-steps',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>MAWB and HAWB:</b> master and house airway bills.','<b>Cut-off:</b> the last time cargo is accepted for the flight.','<b>RCS and known shipper:</b> security status of the cargo and the shipper.','<b>Rolled:</b> cargo that did not travel on the booked flight and moves to the next.','<b>AOG:</b> aircraft on ground, the code for an urgent aircraft part.'])])
X('air-freight-vs-sea-freight',[('Example',['A buyer in Delhi needs 2 tonnes of garments from Dhaka within a week for a launch. By sea it would take weeks, so the answer is air. A month later the same buyer orders 14 tonnes of fabric for next season. Sea freight costs a fraction, and the buyer plans around the transit time. Same buyer, same lane, different answer, and the rule is to decide shipment by shipment.'])])
X('volumetric-weight-air-freight',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>Actual weight:</b> what the packed cargo weighs on the scale.','<b>Volumetric weight:</b> the space the cargo takes, expressed as a weight.','<b>Chargeable weight:</b> the one the airline bills.','<b>Divisor:</b> 6,000 for most general cargo; some express carriers use 5,000.'])])
X('fcl-vs-lcl-shipping',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>CBM:</b> cubic metres, the unit LCL is priced on.','<b>CFS:</b> container freight station, where LCL is stuffed and unstuffed.','<b>Consolidator:</b> the company that combines LCL cargo.','<b>Stuffing and destuffing:</b> loading and unloading a container.','<b>W/M:</b> weight or measurement, the rule that charges on whichever is greater.'])])
X('ocean-freight-surcharges-explained',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>BAF:</b> bunker adjustment factor, for fuel.','<b>CAF:</b> currency adjustment factor.','<b>THC:</b> terminal handling charge, at each end.','<b>PSS:</b> peak season surcharge.','<b>BL fee:</b> the documentation fee for the bill of lading.'])])
X('mundra-port-guide',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>INMUN1:</b> the customs location code for Mundra.','<b>APSEZ:</b> Adani Ports and Special Economic Zone.','<b>Gate-in and gate-out:</b> the times a container enters and leaves the port.','<b>Rail yard:</b> where containers load onto trains for inland depots.','<b>Free time:</b> the days before storage charges start.'])])
X('jnpt-nhava-sheva-port-guide',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>INNSA1:</b> the customs location code for Nhava Sheva.','<b>DPD:</b> direct port delivery.','<b>CFS:</b> container freight station near the port.','<b>Terminal:</b> the operator of a berth and its yard.','<b>Free time:</b> the days before storage charges start.'])])
X('icd-vs-cfs-vs-port-explained',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>ICD:</b> inland container depot, a customs-approved inland terminal.','<b>CFS:</b> container freight station, usually near a port.','<b>Bond movement:</b> the move of cargo under customs control from the port to an inland depot.','<b>Dwell time:</b> how long cargo stays at a terminal.'])])
X('container-types-explained',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>TEU:</b> twenty-foot equivalent unit.','<b>High cube:</b> a container one foot taller than standard.','<b>Payload:</b> the weight of cargo a container may carry.','<b>Tare weight:</b> the weight of the empty container.','<b>Reefer:</b> a refrigerated container.'])])
X('customs-examination-and-out-of-charge',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>RMS:</b> the risk management system that selects bills for checks.','<b>Examination order:</b> the instruction to open and check the cargo.','<b>Test report:</b> a lab report used to confirm what the product is.','<b>Out of charge:</b> release of the goods after duty and checks.'])])
X('bis-certification-for-imports',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>BIS:</b> the Bureau of Indian Standards.','<b>CRS:</b> the compulsory registration scheme for listed electronics and similar products.','<b>ISI mark:</b> the standard mark for products certified under a standard.','<b>Test report:</b> issued by an approved laboratory for the product.'])])
X('express-courier-vs-air-freight',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>Express:</b> door-to-door courier with fast tracked service.','<b>Chargeable weight:</b> the greater of actual and volumetric weight.','<b>Duty paid delivery:</b> the courier pays the duty and bills the receiver.','<b>CTD or courier bill of entry:</b> the simplified customs filing for courier imports.'])])
X('delhi-ncr-icds-tughlakabad-dadri-patparganj',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>INTKD6, INDER6:</b> the customs codes for Tughlakabad and Dadri.','<b>DFC:</b> the dedicated freight corridor for freight trains.','<b>Rake:</b> a full train of container wagons.','<b>Hinterland:</b> the area that a port or depot serves.'])])
X('mundra-vs-jnpt-which-port',[('Terms you will hear',['<b>Hinterland:</b> the region a port serves.','<b>Service:</b> a regular shipping route operated by a line.','<b>Transshipment:</b> cargo changing vessel at an intermediate port.','<b>Landed cost:</b> the total cost of the goods delivered to your door.'])])
